  "전시물 영문해설": {
   "null_rate": 0.0339,
   "unique": 57,
   "top": {
    "Aramid fiber is an extremely strong 'thread'. It has a unique structure with hexagonal carbon rings, making it lightweight yet strong, tough, and resistant to fire. That's why it is widely used in fireproof suits, bulletproof vests, and as reinforcement in construction. Nowadays, it is also being applied in everyday items such as bags. So, make sure to check if there is any aramid fiber around you. Gore-Tex is waterproof, and it allows the vapor of sweat from the body to be expelled from the inside to the outside. This waterproof and moisture-permeable effect is possible because the polymeric material of Teflon is heated and expanded, creating numerous micropores. This molecular structure has pores with a diameter of 0.2 to 10 micrometers, allowing the moisture generated from sweat to be expelled to the outside while preventing the passage of water droplets. Additionally, it has 1 billion 400 million pores per square centimeter, making it lightweight and resistant to temperature changes.": 1,
    "We can observe the structure of the fibers by magnifying the structure of my clothes.": 1,
    "The molecular structure of the most representative natural fiber, cotton fiber, is composed of cellulose. Fibers such as silk, rayon, and pulp, including cotton, have different properties depending on the number of beta-glucose (the basic unit molecule of cellulose) molecules connected. In addition, animal fibers such as wool (composed of keratin) and fur fibers (obtained from beavers and composed of fibroin) are connected by peptide bonds, similar to nylon, resulting in excellent elasticity and strength. Natural fibers and synthetic fibers have differences, but they also have common characteristics.": 1,
    "A spinning machine is a device that makes yarn. Polymer chips (or pellets) are put into the device and melted (fused) at about 150 degrees or more to create thin threads that are passed through a very thin tube. Because each thread is so fine (micro-scale), they are often twisted into bundles to make fabric. Extruders and injection machines also make plastic using a very similar principle to spinning machines.": 1,
    "Step growth polymerization is a method in which functional groups, such as OH and NH2, present at the ends of each molecule, are repetitively linked to form a polymer. Two of the most prominent examples are nylon 6,6 and polyester. Chain growth polymerization is a method in which different functional groups, such as OH and NH2, exist at the ends of a molecule and combine to form a polymer as it grows. Polyacrylic and nylon 6 are the most common polymers.": 1,
    "Both coal and petroleum are not composed of a single substance. They are both made up of various types of hydrocarbon mixtures, which require distillation to separate these mixtures based on their differences in boiling points. Distillation is a method of separating a mixture by heating it to cause evaporation and condensation, which occurs due to the difference in boiling points. This phenomenon is similar to when water condenses on the lid when boiling water at home. In particular, when petroleum is evaporated along with hot steam, the different temperatures at which condensation occurs at each layer of the tower allow for the classification of hydrocarbon mixtures in petroleum as fuel oil, kerosene, diesel, and petrochemical raw materials. Unlike other petroleum products used as fuel for ships, airplanes, and cars, naphtha is used as a raw material for producing polymers.": 1,
    "Wallace Hume Carothers is known as the individual who first synthesized nylon in the world. Furthermore, it is a composite of various polyesters and synthetic rubber, including nylon. Although not widely recognized, he should be acknowledged as the pioneer of the 'plastic' era, which is considered the most crucial pillar in modern society. Please take a moment to indirectly observe the efforts made by Carothers and how he was able to synthesize nylon in 'Carothers' Laboratory'.": 1,
    "The electricity produced through solar panels is in the form of direct current (DC). However, the amount of power generated can vary depending on the surrounding environment, which poses several challenges for direct use. To address these issues, it is necessary to process the generated electricity. Firstly, the produced electricity is measured and managed for usage, storage, and sale through a power control device. The generated electricity is stored in a battery. In cases of insufficient generation or increased power consumption, the battery supplies the lacking power. The electricity produced by solar panels and stored in the battery is supplied as direct current (DC), but it is converted to alternating current (AC) with the appropriate frequency through an inverter to match the rated specifications. This processed electricity can then be used like conventional electricity.": 1,
    "In order to generate electricity in a hydrogen-oxygen fuel cell, both hydrogen and oxygen are required. While oxygen is readily available in the air, obtaining hydrogen in its natural state is difficult. Therefore, a reformer device is used to extract hydrogen from various fuels such as natural gas, methanol, and coal gas. The extracted hydrogen is then delivered to the fuel cell, where it undergoes oxidation and reduction reactions with oxygen in the air to produce electricity. To achieve the desired output, fuel cells are connected in series to form a stack with multiple layers. During this process, high heat is generated, which is utilized for purposes such as heating water and providing heat. The electricity obtained from the fuel cell is in the form of direct current (DC) and is not compatible with the alternating current (AC) that we use. Therefore, it goes through an inverter device to convert it into AC, which is then used for our electrical needs.": 1,
    "Tidal power generation harnesses the difference in tidal currents caused by the tide generating force of the sun and moon on the ocean. Depending on the method of generation, tidal power can be classified into two types: bidirectional flow systems that generate power during both ebb and flood tides, and unidirectional flow systems that generate power only during ebb or flood tides. In bidirectional flow systems, power is generated by creating a difference in water levels between the inside and outside of a turbine through the closure and opening of sluice gates. Unidirectional flow systems can be further divided into ebb tide systems, which generate power during flood tides by closing the sluice gates, and flood tide systems, which generate power during ebb tides by closing the sluice gates. While bidirectional flow systems have higher energy production efficiency, unidirectional flow systems dominate due to the limitations of tidal power generation caused by factors such as the location, topography, and structures of power plants.": 1
   },
